{
  "//": [
    "Mobile Parts Finder — Firestore composite indexes.",
    "Single-field indexes are automatic; only the multi-field queries the app",
    "actually issues are listed here. Deploy with:",
    "   firebase deploy --only firestore:indexes",
    "",
    "Query -> index mapping:",
    "  browse a category, newest groups first    categoryId + groupNo",
    "  browse a category, biggest fitment first  categoryId + memberCount",
    "  category + brand filter                   categoryId + masterBrandId + groupNo",
    "  brand filter across categories            masterBrandId + groupNo",
    "  free-text token search inside a category  categoryId + searchTokens(array)",
    "  brand's models, newest first              brandId + releaseYear",
    "  brand's models A-Z                        brandId + nameLower",
    "",
    "ADMIN BACKEND — added with the admin/analytics layer.",
    "  users:                filter + sort pairs for the admin table, and one",
    "                        single-field index per lower-cased search mirror",
    "                        (mobileShopNameLower, proprietorNameLower,",
    "                        displayNameLower, emailLower, mobileDigits).",
    "  payments/subscriptions: uid + date for a user's history; status + date",
    "                        for the revenue count() and sum() aggregations.",
    "  analyticsEvents:      userId/eventType/sessionId each with timestamp.",
    "  missingModelRequests: status + demand, and the three queue sort orders.",
    "  aiTasks, adminAuditLog: status/type/actor with their timestamps.",
    "",
    "An aggregation query (count, sum) needs the same index an ordinary query",
    "would. Without these the dashboard tiles report themselves unavailable",
    "rather than failing — see api/_services/metrics-service.js countOf()."
  ],
